-- title:
--   Sign interpolating U_q-eigenvalues in the local Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring that is a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal and has finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}(\mathcal O)$, i.e. a $2$-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=(\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q\simeq_{\mathbb Q}\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q)$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible (its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p\in S$, and $N\ge 1$ an integer all of whose prime factors lie in $S$, and assume the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by the integral lattice ([`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), a `Fact`). Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(\mathrm{CuspForm}(\Gamma_0(N),2))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, together with $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$. Assume that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq p$, $q\mid N$, $q^2\nmid N$, at which $\bar\rho$ is not unramified: some valuation subring over $q$ carries an inertia element acting non-trivially. Then there exists an element $u$ of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), the localisation of the base-changed Hecke algebra at the multiplicative set coming from the complement of the prime determined by $\theta$, with the following property. Let $\mathcal O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring that is a domain, adically complete, with finite residue field, which is a module-finite $\mathcal O$-algebra whose structure map is local; let $\psi\colon\mathbb T_\theta\to\mathcal O'$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism; let $M\ge 1$ divide $N$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ that is a newform (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem occurs well at no proper divisor of $M$); let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the level-$M$ Hecke algebra to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$, the $\ell$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $g$, for all primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$; and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O'$ with $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))=\psi(\pi(T_\ell))$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, where $\pi$ is the canonical map of the Hecke algebra into $\mathbb T_\theta$. Then $q\mid M$ and there is an integer $a=\pm1$ with $a_q(g)=a$ in $\mathbb C$ and $\psi(u)=a$ in $\mathcal O'$.
--
--   This is the Galois-theoretic half of the assertion that $U_q$ is redundant in the localised Hecke algebra at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level at which the residual representation is ramified (Wiles, Proposition 2.15; Darmon–Diamond–Taylor, proof of Proposition 4.7): it produces a single element of the anemic local algebra whose value under each point $\psi$ coming from a congruent newform $g$ of level $M\mid N$ is the sign $a_q(g)=\pm1$. It is used in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_sign_forall_point_heckeULin_mul_eq_smul_of_squarefree`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_sign_forall_point_heckeULin_mul_eq_smul_of_squarefree), where this element is matched with the action of $U_q$ on cusp forms.
